- 1 large red pepper, preferably fresh, about the size of a small potato;
- 20-30 ml (about 5 cups) vinegar, or water.
- Pepper, ideally in the shape of a small square, if possible, then mix it into the vinegar and wait until the vinegar is bubbling up from the bottom;
- An empty juice bottle with an opening at one end that contains something like a teaspoon of baking soda;
- Pour the mixture through the end of the bottle and try to pour out onto the top of the lid where the tomatoes are to be placed. The solution should cover the tomato seeds and not the seeds themselves;
- Use the spray bottle to spray the solution down over the tomato seeds and leave them alone.
- If you want to use a sprayer, put it on the top of the glass and press the liquid down on the tomato seeds using the spray bottle.
- If you have a sprayer for your tomato plants, you can place the solution on top of the spray bottle. Then spray it back and forth over the tomato seeds and allow the tomato seeds to soak in the solution for a few seconds before continuing.
